  "plain": "In the 1990s, work applying gauge theory, a branch of mathematics from physics, to economics ran into resistance at Harvard's economics department, according to the researcher Eric Weinstein, who was part of it and who names Pia Malaney in connection with the work. He tells Michels it \"was not taken well,\" especially by Dale Jorgenson, then chairman of the department. He tells it as an example of how establishments push back on new ideas."
